# Layout strategy

> Purpose: pick how layouts behave across mobile · tablet · desktop, then give **every route** its own layout in `route-layouts.mdc`.

## Rules

### The three options (asked when Clients = `web`; `mobile` and `web + mobile` are fixed to `layout`)
| Option | Value | Meaning | Best for | Not for |
|--------|-------|---------|----------|---------|
| **Normal Responsive** | `normal` | One composition that reflows: columns collapse, nav folds. Mobile-friendly website — **not** mobile-app-ready | Marketing, blogs, simple forms, content/SEO-first | App-like/PWA UX, data-heavy dashboards, tablet workflows |
| **Layout Responsive** | `layout` | A different layout per class: mobile app-like (bottom nav, sheets) · tablet mid-density (rail, split panes) · desktop full chrome. One codebase | Web apps, dashboards/admin, `web + mobile`, role-based tools | Tiny throwaway pages |
| **Auto** | `auto` | AI recommends from the concept; dev confirms; result recorded as **Layout resolved** = `normal` \| `layout` \| `mixed` (route groups differ, e.g. marketing `normal` + app `layout`) | Dev is unsure | — |

### Auto — how the AI recommends
| Signal in the concept | Leans |
|-----------------------|-------|
| Mobile / installable / PWA / app-like | `layout` |
| Data-heavy: tables, dashboards, admin, multi-pane, filters, bulk actions | `layout` |
| Roles on different devices (field staff phone, back-office desktop) | `layout` |
| Frequent daily, task-oriented use | `layout` |
| Mostly content/marketing/docs, few routes, SEO-first | `normal` |
| Simple forms, read-only pages | `normal` |
| Public site **and** an app area | `mixed` |

Surface rule: `web + mobile` → **`layout` is required** (one project; Normal Responsive is not available). `mobile` → `layout` (mobile-first). `web` → the dev's choice. Ready folder/shell structure per surface: `project-structure.mdc`.

### Breakpoints
| Class | Range | Design at | Tailwind |
|-------|-------|-----------|----------|
| Mobile | < 768 | 375 | base |
| Tablet | 768–1023 | 768 / 820 | `md:` |
| Desktop | ≥ 1024 | 1280+ | `lg:` / `xl:` |

Nav by class (`layout`): mobile bottom tabs/drawer · tablet nav rail/collapsible side nav · desktop sidebar or top navbar.

## Flow (`format.mdc`)
1. **Ask** the three-way choice in plain language when Clients = `web`. For `mobile` and `web + mobile`, **state** that `layout` applies (and why) instead of asking.
2. **Recommend** as `REC-layout-1` (strategy) — with reasons from the signals above.
3. **Decide → Write** Profile: Layout strategy, Layout resolved, one-line reason.
4. **Derive routes** `R-nn` from the concept (every v1 screen, per role).
5. **Recommend per route** (`REC-route-n`): choose the best pattern from the catalog, then write its mobile · tablet · desktop layout **and its transition** (`transitions.mdc` §2) into `route-layouts.mdc`. `normal` → one composition + reflow notes; `layout` → three explicit layouts; `mixed` → each group follows its mode.
6. **Confirm** — dev approves the map (`APPROVED`) before P2. Later layout changes: edit `route-layouts.mdc` first.

## Pattern catalog (AI picks the best fit per route)
| Pattern | Mobile | Tablet | Desktop |
|---------|--------|--------|---------|
| **Dashboard** | Stacked KPI cards, one chart at a time, bottom tabs | 2-col grid, nav rail | 3–4-col grid, sidebar + top bar, dense widgets |
| **List → Detail** | List page; detail as new page (back) | Split pane | Split pane or table + right drawer, keyboard nav |
| **Data table** | **Card list** (key fields, tap to expand), filter sheet, sticky search | **Condensed table** (priority columns), row → side drawer, filter bar | **Full table**: sticky head, column controls, filter toolbar/sidebar, bulk actions, pagination |
| **Form / wizard** | One column, one step per screen, sticky bottom CTA | Centered card, 1–2 cols, stepper on top | Centered/two-col with live summary aside |
| **Settings / profile** | Grouped list → sub-page per group | Section list left + content | Left nav + content pane |
| **Auth** | Full-screen form, big targets | Centered card | Split screen (form + brand) or centered card |
| **Landing** | Single column, sticky CTA | 2-col sections | Full-width sections, max-width container |
| **Feed / gallery** | Single col / 2-col grid, infinite scroll | 2–3-col grid | 3–4-col grid/masonry, hover previews |
| **Detail / article** | Single column, sticky action bar | Reading width + optional aside | Reading column + sticky aside/TOC |
| **Checkout / confirm** | Stepped, collapsible summary, sticky pay CTA | Two-col (form + summary) | Two-col, sticky summary |

## Do not
- Infer the choice silently, or build P2 screens before `route-layouts.mdc` is `APPROVED`
- Under `normal`: claim the result is mobile-app-ready
- Show a wide desktop table on mobile
